<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladeshi banks to stop loans against shares.</title>
<headline>Bangladeshi banks to stop loans against shares.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's central bank has asked commercial banks to stop offering loans against securities as collateral, officials with commercial banks said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;This means the offering of the credit against shares will be stopped,&quot; one official said.</p>
<p>The central Bangladesh Bank in late 1994 allowed commercial banks to give credit at a rate of 40 percent of the market value of shares, for amounts up to one million taka ($23,600).</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
</text>
